            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-operads"} (∞,1)-operads
            regarding these as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} ∞Grpd-enriched
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operads"} operads
          %p
            It is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad"} operadic
            analog of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+Segal+categories"} model structure for Segal categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+objects"} fibrant objects
            are operadic analogs of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal+categories"} Segal categories
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            for the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tree+category"} tree category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+sets"} dendroidal sets
          %h3#segal_operads Segal operads
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
            for the tree with a single edge and no vertices. Write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi sdSet
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi sSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  sdSet := [\Omega^{op}, sSet]
          %p
            for the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaves"} simplicial presheaves
            on the tree category –
            %em simplicial dendroidal sets
            or
            %em dendroidal simplicial sets
            (see
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+complete+dendroidal+Segal+spaces"} model structure for complete dendroidal Segal spaces
            for more on this).
          #InclusionOfSegalPreOperads.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong Segal pre-operad
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in [\Omega^{op}, sSet]
              is a simplicial dendroidal set such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi η
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X(\eta)
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+object"} discrete
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
              (a plain set regarded as a simplicially constant simplicial set). Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SegalPreOperad
                    %mo ↪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    SegalPreOperad \hookrightarrow [\Omega^{op}, sSet]
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              on the Segal pre-operads.
            %p
              A
              %strong Segal operad
              is a Segal pre-operad such that for every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tree"} tree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \in \Omega
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/powering"} powering
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi Sp
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi sSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X^{\Omega[T]} \to X^{Sp(T)}
                    \\in
                    sSet
            %p
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spine"} spine
              inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Sp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Sp(T) \hookrightarrow T) \in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+set"} dSet
              into
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} acyclic
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibration"} Kan fibration
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SegalOperad
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi SegalPreOperad
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    SegalOperad \hookrightarrow SegalPreOperad
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              on the Segal operads.
            %p
              A
              %strong Reedy-fibrant Segal operad
              is a Segal operad which is moreover fibrant in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+Reedy+model+structure"} generalized Reedy model structure
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi sSet
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi gReedy
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Omega^{op}, sSet]_{gReedy}
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#CisinskiMoerdijk"}> Cisinski-Moerdijk, def. 7.1, def. 8.1
            ).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The definition of Segal pre-operads encodes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              of colors of an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad"} operad
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tree"} tree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
              of operations in the operad of the shape of this tree — notably
              = succeed "-groupoids" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              = succeed "-ary" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "-corolla," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T = C_n
            %p
              The condition on Segal operads encodes the existence of
              %em composition
              of these operad operations by
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-anafunctors"} ∞-anafunctors
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal+category"} Segal category
              for more on this.
            %p The Reedy fibrancy condition is mostly a technical convenience.
          .num_prop
            %h6#obervation Obervation
            %p
              The inclusion def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InclusionOfSegalPreOperads"}
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sdSet
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %munder
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi γ
                              %mo *
                        %mover
                          %mo ←
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi γ
                              %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi γ
                            %mo !
                    %mi SegalPreOperad
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    sdSet
                    \\stackrel{\overset{\gamma_!}{\to}}{\stackrel{\overset{\gamma^*}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{\gamma_*}{\to}}}
                    SegalPreOperad
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              One way to see the existence of the adjoints is to note that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SegalPreOperad
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SegalPreOperad
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(\Omega)
              which is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega \times \Delta
              at morphisms of the form
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi Id
                        %mi η
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-,Id_\eta)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
              is the tree with one edge and no vertex. Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                    %mo :
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo →
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\gamma : \Delta \times \Omega \to S(\Omega)
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
              functor, then the inclusion of Segal pre-operads is the precomposition with this functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi γ
                      %mo *
                    %mo :
                    %mi SegalPreOperad
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Ω
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ↪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\gamma^* : SegalPreOperad \simeq [S(\Omega)^{op}, sSet] \hookrightarrow [\Omega^{op}, sSet]
                    \\,.
            %p
              Therefore the left and right adjoint to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi γ
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma^*
              are given by left and right
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extension"} Kan extension
              along
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi γ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
            %p Explicitly, these adjoints are given as follows.
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi sSet
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in [\Omega^{op}, sSet]
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mo !
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma_!(X)
              sends a tree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              either to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X(T)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              is non-linear, hence if it admits no morphism to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi η
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi η
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi T
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi π
                              %mn 0
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi η
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi γ
                              %mo !
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi T
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X(\eta) &amp;\to&amp; X(T)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\pi_0 X(\eta) &amp;\to&amp; \gamma_!(X)(T)
                    }
            %p
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo →
                    %mi η
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X(T \to \eta)
              for the unique morphism to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi η
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
            %p
              In words,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mo !
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma_!(X)
              is obtained from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              precisely by contracting the simplicial set of colors to its set of connected components.
          %h3#special_morphisms Special morphisms
          %p We discuss morphisms between Segal pre-operads with special properties, which will appear in the model structure.
          #NormalMonomorphism.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              Say a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SegalPreOperad
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SegalPreOperad
              is a
              %strong normal monomorphism
              precisely if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi γ
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma^*(f)
              is a normal monomorphism (see
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+Reedy+model+structure"} generalized Reedy model structure
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+sets"} dendroidal sets
              (see there for details).
            %p
              Correspondingly, a Segal pro-operad
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is called
              %em normal
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset \to X
              is a normal monomorphism.
          #PreOperadAcyclicFibration.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              A morphism in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SegalPreOperad
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SegalPreOperad
              is called an
              %strong acyclic fibration
              precisely if it has the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
              against all normal monomorphisms, def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NormalMonomorphism"}
          #SegalWeakEquivalence.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              Say a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SegalPreOperad
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SegalPreOperad
              is a
              %em Segal weak equivalence
              precisely if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi γ
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma^*(f)
              is a weak equivalence in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+dendroidal+complete+Segal+spaces"} model structure for dendroidal complete Segal spaces
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi op
                      %mi m
                      %mo ,
                      %mi sSet
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                          %mrow
                            %mi gReedy
                          %mrow
                            %mi cSegal
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Omega^{op}m, sSet]_{gReedy \atop cSegal}
          #WeakEquivalencesAndFibrations.num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              Call a morphism in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SegalPreOperad
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SegalPreOperad
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a weak equivalence precisely if it is a Segal weak equivalence, def.
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SegalWeakEquivalence"}
              %li
                %p
                  a cofibration precisely if it is a normal monomorphism, def.
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NormalMonomorphism"}
          %p
            Theorem
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExistenceOfTheModelStructure"}
            below asserts that this is indeed a model category struture whose fibrant objects are the Segal operads.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#of_the_various_classes_of_morphisms Of the various classes of morphisms
          .num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Omega^{op}, sSet]
              is a normal monomorphism and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi η
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi η
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0 X(\eta) \to \pi_0 Y(\eta)
              is a monomorphism, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mo !
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma_!(f)
              is normal in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi SegalPreOperad
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SegalPreOperad
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#CisinskiMoerdijk"}> Cis-Moer, lemma 7.4
            ).
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The class of normal monomorphisms in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SegalPreOperad
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SegalPreOperad
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} generated
              (under
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transfinite+composition"} transfinite composition
              and
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retracts"} retracts
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mo !
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∪
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ×
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mo !
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo ,
                        %mi T
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo ,
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo →
                    %mi η
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\{
                    \\gamma_!(\partial \Delta[n] \times \Omega[T]  \cup \Delta[n] \times \partial \Omega[T])
                    \\to
                    \\gamma_! (\Delta[n], \Omega[T])
                    \\}_{n \in \Delta, T \in \Omega, {\vert T\vert} \geq 1}
                    \\cup
                    \\{
                    \\emptyset \to \eta
                    \\}
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#CisinskiMoerdijk"}> Cis-Moer, prop 7.5
            ).
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                        %mrow
                          %mi gReedy
                        %mrow
                          %mi Segal
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in [\Omega^{op}, sSet]_{gReedy \atop Segal}
              be fibrant. Then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mo *
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma_* X
              is a Reedy fibrant Segal operad. If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is moreover fibrant in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                        %mrow
                          %mi gReedy
                        %mrow
                          %mi cSegal
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Omega^{op}, sSet]_{gReedy \atop cSegal}
              then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} counit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi γ
                      %mo *
                    %mi γ
                    %mo *
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma^* \gamma* X \to X
              is a weak equivalence in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi sSet
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                          %mrow
                            %mi gReedy
                          %mrow
                            %mi cSegal
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Omega^{op}, sSet]_{gReedy \atop cSegal}
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#CisinskiMoerdijk"}> Cis-Moer, prop 8.2
            ).
          #AcyclicFibrationsAreIndeedWeakEquivalences.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_2 Lemma
            %p
              An acyclic fibration in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi SegalPreOperad
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SegalPreOperad
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PreOperadAcyclicFibration"}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi sSet
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                          %mrow
                            %mi gReedy
                          %mrow
                            %mi Segal
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Omega^{op}, sSet]_{gReedy \atop Segal}
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#CisinskiMoerdijk"}> Cis-Moer, prop 8.12
            ).
          %h3#of_the_model_structure_itself Of the model structure itself
          #ExistenceOfTheModelStructure.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              The structures in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WeakEquivalencesAndFibrations"}
              make the category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SegalPreOperad
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SegalPreOperad
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              which is
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"}> cofibrantly generated
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+proper+model+category"}> left proper
                  \.
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#CisinskiMoerdijk"}> Cis-Moer, theorem 8.13
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              The existence of the cofibrantly generated model structure follows with
              = succeed ":" do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "combinatorial+model+category#SmithTheorem"} Smith’s theorem
            %ol
              %li
                %p the Segal equivalences are an accessibly embedded accessible full subcategory of the arrow category;
              %li
                %p the acyclic cofibrations are closed under pushout and retract;
                %p
                  (both of these because these morphisms come from the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial model category
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msup
                            %mi Ω
                            %mi op
                          %mo ,
                          %mi sSet
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mi gReedy
                              %mrow
                                %mi cSegal
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Omega^{op}, sSet]_{gReedy \atop cSegal}
              %li
                %p
                  the morphisms with right lifting against the normal monomorphisms are weak equivalences, by lemma
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AcyclicFibrationsAreIndeedWeakEquivalences"}
          %h3#relation_to_other_model_structures Relation to other model structures
          %p
            We discuss the relation to various other model structures for operads. For an overview see
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/table+-+models+for+%28infinity%2C1%29-operads"} table - models for (infinity,1)-operads
          %h4#to_dendroidal_complete_segal_spaces To dendroidal complete Segal spaces
          %p
            (…)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+dendroidal+complete+Segal+spaces"} model structure for dendroidal complete Segal spaces
          %h2#references References
          %ul#CisinskiMoerdijk
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"}> Denis-Charles Cisinski
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
              %em Dendroidal Segal spaces and infinity-operads
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1010.4956"}> arXiv:1010.4956
              )
